Assignment: Data Preprocessing Based on Column Types
Course: Machine Learning
Topic: Data Preprocessing Based on Column Types
Total Marks: 30
Submission: Python (.ipynb) + Report (PDF/Word)
Objective

The objective of this assignment is to understand different types of dataset columns and apply appropriate preprocessing techniques using Python and Pandas.

Dataset

You may use any CSV dataset containing:

Continuous numerical columns
Discrete numerical columns
Nominal categorical columns
Ordinal categorical columns
Boolean columns

Example datasets:

Titanic Dataset
Employee Dataset
Student Dataset
Customer Dataset
Task 1: Identify Column Types (5 Marks)

Load the dataset and identify each column as one of the following:

Column Name	Type
Age	Continuous Numerical
Salary	Continuous Numerical
Gender	Nominal
Education	Ordinal
Purchased	Boolean
Task 2: Continuous Numerical Columns (5 Marks)

Perform preprocessing on all continuous numerical columns.

Required Tasks
Detect missing values.
Fill missing values using:
Mean
Median
Detect outliers.
Handle outliers using any suitable method.
Apply feature scaling.
Compare Min-Max Scaling and Standardization.
Questions
Which columns are continuous?
Which missing value technique did you use?
Why did you choose Mean or Median?
Which scaling method worked better?
Task 3: Discrete Numerical Columns (4 Marks)

Perform preprocessing on discrete numerical columns.

Required Tasks
Detect missing values.
Fill missing values.
Detect invalid values.
Check for outliers.
Apply scaling if necessary.
Questions
Which columns are discrete?
Are there any invalid values?
Did you apply scaling? Why?
Task 4: Nominal Categorical Columns (5 Marks)

Perform preprocessing on nominal categorical columns.

Required Tasks
Find missing values.
Fill missing values using Mode.
Apply One-Hot Encoding.
Merge rare categories (if needed).
Questions
Which columns are nominal?
Why is One-Hot Encoding preferred?
What problem occurs if Label Encoding is applied to nominal data?
Task 5: Ordinal Categorical Columns (4 Marks)

Perform preprocessing on ordinal columns.

Required Tasks

Suppose the dataset contains:

Education
Primary
Secondary
Bachelor
Master
PhD

Encode them as:

Category	Value
Primary	1
Secondary	2
Bachelor	3
Master	4
PhD	5
Questions
Why should ordinal data not use One-Hot Encoding?
What happens if the order is changed?
Task 6: Boolean Columns (3 Marks)

Convert all Boolean columns into numeric values.

Example

Original	Converted
Yes	1
No	0
True	1
False	0
Questions
Which Boolean columns exist?
Why are Boolean values converted into numbers?
Task 7: Data Visualization (2 Marks)

Visualize your dataset before and after preprocessing.

Use at least four of the following:

Histogram
Box Plot
Count Plot (or Bar Chart)
Pie Chart
Scatter Plot
Heatmap (optional)

Include screenshots in your report.

Task 8: Final Dataset (2 Marks)

Display the final cleaned dataset.

Verify that:

No missing values remain.
All categorical variables are encoded.
Numerical columns are scaled (where required).
Boolean values are numeric.
Submission Requirements

Submit:

Python Notebook (.ipynb)
PDF/Word Report containing:
Dataset description
Screenshots of preprocessing steps
Visualizations
Final cleaned dataset
Answers to all questions
Bonus Task (+5 Marks)

Perform the following:

Remove duplicate rows.
Detect highly correlated features using a correlation matrix.
Apply Log Transformation on a highly skewed numerical column.
Explain why log transformation was useful.
Compare the dataset before and after preprocessing using charts.
